## 3. Farmer Dashboard

> **Audience**: Low-tech farmers. Big text. Simple language. Malay/English labels ok. Actionable: "What should I plant? Is fertilizer expensive?"

### 3.1 Layout (Top to Bottom)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HEADER BAR (sticky)                                         │
│  🌱 FoodMonitor Farmer   [Tab: Prices | Input Cost | News | AI]│
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ HERO BANNER — "Food Risk Level" gauge + 1-sentence summary  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ TAB CONTENT (full width)                                     │
│                                                              │
│ [Default: Prices tab]                                        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
│ FOOTER — data source provenance + last updated               │
```

### 3.2 Header Bar

- **Logo**: 🌱 icon + "FoodMonitor" + "Farmer" badge in green pill
- **Tabs**: `Prices` | `Input Cost` | `News` | `AI Advisor` (English-primary; mixed Malay in descriptions/tooltips is fine)
- **Right side**: Data freshness indicator → call `trpc.liveData.getStatus` → green dot if latest job `success: true` within 24h, amber if >24h, red if failed

### 3.3 Hero Banner (Always Visible Above Tabs)

> **API**: `trpc.risk.getCfsr`

- **Left**: Semicircle gauge showing `cfsr` score (0-100)
  - 0-33 GREEN "Safe"
  - 34-66 AMBER "Caution"
  - 67-100 RED "High Risk"
- **Right**: One plain-language sentence:
  - `riskBand === "LOW"` → "Food supply is stable. Good time to plan new crops."
  - `riskBand === "MODERATE"` → "Some disruptions detected. Monitor input costs."
  - `riskBand === "HIGH"` / `"CRITICAL"` → "Significant disruptions. Check fertilizer and prices."
- **Provenance footer**: `computedAt` from response + "Based on {dataSourcesSummary}"
- **Click to expand**: Shows 5 component scores as simple bar chart → `components.n1ImportDependency` etc.

### 3.4 Tab 1: Prices

> **APIs**: `trpc.prices.getCurrent` + `trpc.prices.getTrend`
> **No-repeat rule**: Show each commodity once. Price shown here = NOT repeated in Input Cost tab.

#### Level 0 — Price Cards Grid (3 columns desktop, 1 mobile)

For each item returned by `trpc.prices.getCurrent.useQuery()`:

| Element | Source | Display |
|---|---|---|
| Commodity name | `commodityName` | Bold, 16px |
| Current price | `priceMyr` | Large number, `RM X.XX` |
| Unit | `unitCanonical` | Small text beside price, e.g. "per kg" |
| Trend arrow | Computed from `trendPct` (call `getTrend` for top 6 items) | ↑ red if >0, ↓ green if <0 |
| Trend % | `trendPct` from `getTrend` | "+5.2% in 7 days" |

**Which items to show**: Call `trpc.prices.getCurrent.useQuery()` (no item filter) → get top 20 national_median prices. Group into:
1. **Staples**: rice, wheat, cooking oil, sugar (filter by `commodityName` containing those keywords)
2. **Vegetables**: kangkung, bayam, tomato, cabbage
3. **Protein**: chicken, egg, fish

#### Level 1 — Click Card → Expand

- Show 30-day sparkline chart from `trpc.prices.getTrend.useQuery({ item: commodityName, days: 30 })`
- Show `data` array as line chart
- Show `trendPct` as summary

#### Level 2 — Source

- Show "Source: PriceCatcher (Data.gov.my)" from `_meta.source`
- Show "Last updated: {date of latest row}"

### 3.5 Tab 2: Input Cost

> **APIs**: `trpc.risk.getDashboardIndices` (inputCostStress, globalCommodityStress) + `trpc.risk.getFuzzyState` (fertilizer status)
> **No-repeat rule**: This tab shows STRESS INDICES and FUZZY STATES. Not raw prices (those are in Tab 1).

#### Level 0 — Two Cards Side by Side

**Card A: Input Cost Stress**
| Element | Source |
|---|---|
| Score gauge (0-100) | `dashboardIndices.inputCostStress.score` |
| Label | "Input Cost Stress" |
| Status badge | `inputCostStress.status` → "observed" / "derived" / "missing" |
| Coverage | `inputCostStress.coverage` as percentage |
| Plain text | Score > 70 → "Fertilizer and fuel costs are very high" / Score 40-70 → "Input costs are elevated" / Score < 40 → "Input costs are normal" |

**Card B: Global Commodity Stress**
| Element | Source |
|---|---|
| Score gauge (0-100) | `dashboardIndices.globalCommodityStress.score` |
| Label | "Global Food Price Stress" |
| Plain text | Similar thresholded message |

#### Level 1 — Expand Either Card

**Input Cost expanded**:
- Show `inputCostStress.source` ("commodity_prices fertilizer/fuel benchmarks")
- Show fuzzy state for fertilizer: `fuzzyState.fertilizer` → "low" / "medium" / "high" / "very_high"
- Show fuzzy compound state: `fuzzyState.compound`

**Global Commodity expanded**:
- Show `globalCommodityStress.source` ("commodity_prices World Bank benchmarks")

#### Level 2 — Source Provenance
- Data source string from `.source` field
- `fuzzyState.computedAt` timestamp

### 3.6 Tab 3: News

> **API**: `trpc.news.getLatest.useQuery({ limit: 10, side: "producer" })`
> **Filter**: `sentimentSide === "producer"` to show farmer-relevant news only

#### Level 0 — News Feed

For each article:
| Element | Source |
|---|---|
| Title | `title` (truncate to 80 chars) |
| Source name | `source` |
| Time | `publishedAt` → relative ("2 hours ago") |
| Alert badge | If `isAlert === true` → red "AMARAN" badge |
| Severity pill | `severity` → colour coded |
| Commodity tag | `primaryCommodity` if present |

#### Level 1 — Click Article

- Show `implication` text (full)
- Show `sentimentScore` as gauge (-1 to +1)
- Link to original article: `url`

#### Level 2 — Source Metadata
- `insightScore`, `severity`, `sentimentSide`
- `_meta.source`

### 3.7 Tab 4: AI Advisor

> **API**: `trpc.ai.getAnalysis.useQuery({ type: "recommendations" })`

#### Level 0
- Display `content` as rendered Markdown
- Label: "AI Recommendations — last updated {generatedAt}"

#### Level 1
- Show `structuredOutput` if available (JSON rendered as cards)

#### Level 2
- Show `dataContext` — what data went into generating this
- Show `promptHash` for audit trail

