## 4. Government Dashboard

> **Audience**: Policy officers, ministry staff. More data-dense but still clean. Tables ok. Trend comparisons needed.

### 4.1 Layout

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HEADER BAR (sticky full-width)                                    │
│  🛡️ FoodMonitor Government   CFSR: [72] CRITICAL                  │
│  [Tab: Overview | Price Intel | Supply Risk | News | AI Analysis] │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ TAB CONTENT (full width, no max-width)                            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
│ FOOTER — provenance, data sources, last ingestion status          │
```

### 4.2 Header Bar

- **Logo**: 🛡️ + "FoodMonitor" + "Government" badge
- **CFSR Badge**: `trpc.risk.getCfsr` → `cfsr` value + `riskBand` colour pill
- **Component mini-bar**: 5 tiny numbers inline `N1:{n1} N2:{n2} N3:{n3} N4:{n4} N5:{n5}` from `components`
- **Data status**: `trpc.liveData.getStatus` → green/amber/red dot
- Full-width, `position: sticky`

### 4.3 Tab 1: Overview

> **APIs**: `trpc.risk.getCfsr` + `trpc.risk.getCfsrHistory` + `trpc.risk.getDashboardIndices` + `trpc.risk.getFuzzyState`
> **No-repeat rule**: CFSR shown here only. Dashboard indices shown here. Not repeated in other tabs.

#### Row 1: CFSR Hero (full-width card)

| Element | Source |
|---|---|
| CFSR score | `getCfsr().cfsr` |
| Risk band | `getCfsr().riskBand` |
| Delta | `getCfsr().delta` → "+2.3 from yesterday" |
| Confidence | `getCfsr().scoreConfidence` as percentage |
| Coverage | `getCfsr().scoreCoverage` as percentage |
| Data sources | `getCfsr().dataSourcesSummary` |
| Computed at | `getCfsr().computedAt` |

Right side: 30-day trend chart → `trpc.risk.getCfsrHistory.useQuery({ days: 30 })` → line chart of `cfsr` over time

#### Row 2: Component Breakdown (5 columns)

For each component in `getCfsr().components`:

| Component | Field | Label |
|---|---|---|
| N1 | `n1ImportDependency` | Import Dependency |
| N2 | `n2SupplyChainHealth` | Supply Chain |
| N3 | `n3FertilizerAvailability` | Fertilizer |
| N4 | `n4GeopoliticalRisk` | Geopolitical |
| N5 | `n5PriceVolatility` | Price Volatility |

Each as vertical bar or circular progress with colour thresholds:
- 0-30 green, 31-50 amber, 51-70 orange, 71-100 red

Expand → show `componentMeta[componentKey]` if available

#### Row 3: Dashboard Indices (6 cards, 3×2 grid)

> **API**: `trpc.risk.getDashboardIndices`

| Index | Field | Label |
|---|---|---|
| Retail Price Stress | `retailPriceStress` | "Are retail prices abnormally high?" |
| State Price Dispersion | `statePriceDispersion` | "How much do prices vary between states?" |
| Input Cost Stress | `inputCostStress` | "Are fertilizer/fuel costs elevated?" |
| Global Commodity Stress | `globalCommodityStress` | "Are world market prices elevated?" |
| News Attention | `newsAttention` | "How much crisis-related news coverage?" |
| Data Quality | `dataQuality` | "How fresh and complete is our data?" |

Each card shows:
- `score` (0-100) as circular gauge
- `coverage` as progress bar
- `status` badge: "observed" (green) / "derived" (amber) / "missing" (red)
- `source` string as small text
- `latestCanonicalDate` for dataQuality card

#### Row 4: Fuzzy State Summary (single card)

> **API**: `trpc.risk.getFuzzyState`

| Element | Source |
|---|---|
| Fertilizer State | `fertilizer` ("low"/"medium"/"high"/"very_high") |
| Price Trend State | `priceTrend` ("falling"/"stable"/"rising"/"surging") |
| News Volume State | `newsVolume` ("quiet"/"normal"/"elevated"/"high") |
| Compound State | `compound` overall label |
| Conflicts | `conflicts` JSON array → list detected conflicts |
| Membership Scores | `membershipScores` → expandable detail |

### 4.4 Tab 2: Price Intelligence

> **APIs**: `trpc.prices.getCurrent` + `trpc.prices.getTrend`
> **No-repeat rule**: Raw price data lives HERE. Dashboard indices (summary stress scores) live in Overview tab only.

#### Section A: Current National Median Prices (Table)

Call `trpc.prices.getCurrent.useQuery()` → filter `seriesType === 'national_median'`

| Column | Source |
|---|---|
| Commodity | `commodityName` |
| Price (RM) | `priceMyr` |
| Price (USD) | `priceUsd` (if World Bank row) |
| Unit | `unitCanonical` |
| Date | `date` |
| Source | `sourceId` ("pricecatcher" or "worldbank_rtfp") |

Sortable by any column. Searchable by commodity name.

#### Section B: Price Trend Explorer

- Dropdown/search to pick commodity name
- Call `trpc.prices.getTrend.useQuery({ item: selectedCommodity, days: 30 })`
- Show line chart + `trendPct` value
- Below chart: "Source: {_meta.source}, series: {_meta.series ?? 'national_median'}"

#### Section C: World Bank Commodity Prices

Call `trpc.prices.getCurrent.useQuery()` → rows where data includes `displayName, category, subcategory, priceUsd`

| Column | Source |
|---|---|
| Commodity | `displayName` |
| Category | `category` / `subcategory` |
| Price (USD) | `priceUsd` |
| Unit | `unit` |
| Source URL | `sourceUrl` (clickable) |
| Workbook Updated | `workbookUpdatedAt` |

### 4.5 Tab 3: Supply Risk

> **APIs**: `trpc.risk.getCfsr` (components only — N1, N2, N3, N4) + `trpc.risk.getFuzzyState` (conflicts)
> **No-repeat rule**: This tab shows supply-chain NARRATIVE and CONFLICTS. Component SCORES shown in Overview, not repeated here as numbers — only referenced contextually.

#### Section A: Risk Narrative

Call `trpc.ai.getAnalysis.useQuery({ type: "cfsr_analysis" })`
- Render `content` as Markdown
- Label: "AI-Generated Supply Risk Assessment"
- Show `generatedAt`

#### Section B: Fuzzy Logic Conflicts

From `trpc.risk.getFuzzyState` → `conflicts` array
- Each conflict as an alert card
- Show `membershipScores` breakdown

#### Section C: Data Pipeline Health

Call `trpc.liveData.getStatus`
- Table of recent ingestion runs
- Columns: Job name, Status (success/fail), Started, Duration, Rows Written, Error
- Colour-code: green rows = success, red = fail

### 4.6 Tab 4: News & Alerts

> **API**: `trpc.news.getLatest.useQuery({ limit: 50 })`
> **No-repeat rule**: News data shown HERE only. Not duplicated in other tabs.

#### Level 0: Alert Ribbon

Filter articles where `isAlert === true` → horizontal scrolling ribbon at top
Each alert: severity badge + title + commodity tag

#### Level 0: Summary Stats (4 cards)

Computed from news response:
| Card | Computation |
|---|---|
| Total Articles | `data.length` |
| Alerts Count | `data.filter(a => a.isAlert).length` |
| Avg Sentiment | `mean(data.map(a => a.sentimentScore))` |
| Top Commodity | `mode(data.map(a => a.primaryCommodity))` |

#### Level 1: News Table (sortable, filterable)

| Column | Source |
|---|---|
| Title | `title` (clickable → `url`) |
| Source | `source` |
| Published | `publishedAt` |
| Severity | `severity` (colour pill) |
| Sentiment | `sentimentScore` (colour bar) |
| Side | `sentimentSide` |
| Commodity | `primaryCommodity` |
| Insight Score | `insightScore` |
| Alert? | `isAlert` (boolean icon) |

Filters: dropdown for `severity`, `sentimentSide`, `primaryCommodity`

#### Level 2: Click Row → Detail

- Full `implication` text
- If reasoning metadata available: `matchedKeywords`, `foodSecurityRelevance`, `eventType`, `sourceAuthority`, `analysisConfidence`

### 4.7 Tab 5: AI Analysis

> **APIs**: `trpc.ai.getAnalysis` (3 different types)
> **No-repeat rule**: AI analysis shown HERE only.

#### Three expandable sections:

**Section A: CFSR Analysis**
- `trpc.ai.getAnalysis.useQuery({ type: "cfsr_analysis" })`
- Rendered Markdown
- Metadata: `generatedAt`, `dataContext`

**Section B: Recommendations**
- `trpc.ai.getAnalysis.useQuery({ type: "recommendations" })`
- Rendered Markdown
- Metadata: same

**Section C: Gap Analysis**
- `trpc.ai.getAnalysis.useQuery({ type: "gap_analysis" })`
- Rendered Markdown
- Metadata: same

